  "final_text": "All four steps are done. The rule reads back as enabled.\n\n- **Data view:** the time field on 'Kibana Sample Data Logs' is `timestamp`. `response` is a string field, so I used `response.keyword` for the response-code panel and the rule.\n- **Dashboard:** 'S4-52a4ec68 Web logs' has two panels. One is a line chart of requests over time, and the other is a bar chart of requests by response code.\n- **Alert rule:** 'S4-52a4ec68 5xx errors' checks every minute. It fires when more than 10 requests have `response.keyword` from \"500\" to \"599\" within 5 minutes. The range is a string comparison, which covers every 5xx code because they are all three-digit strings. The rule was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n- **Panel edit:** the response-code panel is now titled 'Responses by code'. I didn't read the dashboard back afterwards to confirm the new title.\n- **Read-back:** the rule shows `enabled: true` and status `ok`.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
